# Function window design (unified style)

**Purpose:** every Tools parameter dialog looks and behaves the same
(BLAST / Align / Mapping / Flexidot / TE-Aid / MSA plot / Tree, and new tools).

**Canonical code:** `TOOL_PARAMS_*` and helpers in
`repeatviewer/views/tool_dialogs.py`. Prefer those helpers — do not reinvent layouts.

---

## How to invoke this rule (keywords)

Say any of these in the chat when designing or editing a tool dialog:

- **function window** / **function windows**
- **tool params dialog** / **Align-style dialog** / **BLAST-style dialog**
- **follow the layout rule** / **tool-params-dialog-layout**
- **Options tab** + **Executables** / **Process output** / **Advanced Settings**
- **dialog width 608** / **field width 260**

Also auto-applies when editing files matching the globs above.

---

## Shared constants (exact numbers)

| Constant | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `TOOL_PARAMS_DIALOG_WIDTH` | **608** | Dialog width (minimum + fit/resize) |
| `TOOL_PARAMS_FIELD_WIDTH` | **260** | Settings / Advanced combo & spinbox width |
| `TOOL_PARAMS_LABEL_COLUMN_REF` | `"Minimum alignment length:"` | Shared label-column width (font metrics) |

Other fixed spacings used everywhere:

| Element | Value |
|---|---|
| Root dialog margins | **22, 18, 22, 16** (L, T, R, B) |
| Root dialog spacing | **8** |
| Parameters page margins | **16, 10, 16, 10** |
| Parameters page spacing | **4** |
| Form label ↔ field (horizontal) | **12** |
| Form row spacing (vertical) | **4** |
| Section separator host height | **7** (1 px mid line, margins 0,2,0,2) |
| Mode / Inputs radio spacing | **2** |
| Options page margins | **16, 14, 16, 14** |
| Options group-box spacing | **14** |
| Options Right-click radio spacing | **6** |
| Executables group margins | **10, 8, 10, 8** |
| Executables row spacing | **8** |
| PATH status under checkbox | spacing **2**; flush left (no 24 px indent) |
| Process output inner margins | **12, 10, 12, 10** |
| Process output checkbox spacing | **6** |
| Footer button spacing | **8** |
| Checkbox tick ↔ label (stylesheet) | **6 px** |

---

## 1. Tabs (always on top)

Like BLAST: **BLASTn | BLASTp | BLASTx | Options**.

Rules:

1. Function / engine / program tabs first (e.g. Minimap2 | HISAT2, MAFFT | MUSCLE | FastGA).
2. Last tab is always **Options**.
3. `QTabBar` (or `QTabWidget` tab bar): `setExpanding(False)`, `setDocumentMode(True)`.
4. Hide the **Advanced Settings** footer button on the Options tab.
5. Non-modal open when Define inputs must accept Files-panel clicks
   (`_present_te_viz_dialog` / same pattern as Align).

---

## 2. Normal tabs (not Options) — page body

**Order of sections** (omit any that the tool does not need; do not invent extra
top-level section names):

1. **Mode** — combine / separate / plot mode / …  
2. **Inputs** — Use selected sequences / Define inputs (+ path rows)  
3. **Outputs** — format, write flags, …  
4. **Settings** — primary run parameters  
5. **Advanced Settings** — *not* a permanent section on the page; content lives in a
   collapsible panel revealed by the footer **Advanced Settings ▸** button

Between major sections: bold title `QLabel("<b>Inputs</b>")` +
`_form_section_separator()`.

**Distance between sections** (Mode → Inputs → Outputs → Settings): the separator
block is **7 px** tall; page `spacing` is **4**; form vertical spacing is **4**.
Keep these — do not add large custom spacers that make one tool look looser than
another.

### Page + form metrics

| Layout | Margins | Spacing |
|---|---|---|
| Page `QVBoxLayout` | **16, 10, 16, 10** | **4** |
| `QFormLayout` | **0, 0, 0, 0** | H **12**, V **4** |

- Label alignment: `AlignRight | AlignVCenter`
- Option fields: `FieldsStayAtSizeHint` + fixed width **260**
- Path / Reference / Define-inputs rows may use `ExpandingFieldsGrow` so Browse lines up

### Label column (mandatory — same across all tools)

Field column must start on the **same vertical line** in every function window:

1. Width = `fontMetrics().horizontalAdvance(TOOL_PARAMS_LABEL_COLUMN_REF)`.
2. Call **`sync_form_field_column_spacers(...)`** after build, on `showEvent`, and when
   Define inputs toggles.
3. Mode / Inputs radios and lone checkboxes use spacer `QLabel("")` — never bare
   `addRow("", widget)`.
4. Colon labels (`"Threads:"`) are right-aligned inside that width.
5. Do not use a per-dialog longer `ref_label` that widens one window.

### Controls

- Combos / spins: **`NoWheelComboBox` / `NoWheelSpinBox`** (no mouse-wheel value change)
  at width **260**. Same width in Advanced as in Settings.
- Shorten long combo *display* text; put detail in `?` (`field_with_help` /
  `label_with_help`).
- Define inputs: `TeMultiInputFilesWidget`; placeholder
  `Click in Files/Folders or Browse…`.
- Help `?`: after the control by default; on the **label** when Browse must stay
  flush (path rows). Database/Genome + Manage: `?` on the combo row only.

Exception: TE-Aid hit % rows stay compact (~100 px + swatch), not 260.

### Advanced Settings (footer, not a page section)

- Footer left: **Restore Defaults** then **Advanced Settings ▸** (checkable;
  **▸** collapsed / **▾** expanded; pointing-hand cursor).
- Panel starts hidden (`maximumHeight 0`); expand grows the dialog; collapse
  shrinks to compact content.
- Advanced form top margin **0, 4, 0, 0**.
- Hide this button on Options.

---

## 3. Options tab (always)

**Group order** (include only what applies; order is fixed):

1. **Right-click action** — **always** present  
2. **Executables** — if the tool uses external binaries  
3. **Process output** — if the tool runs a subprocess worth monitoring  

| Layout | Value |
|---|---|
| Page margins | **16, 14, 16, 14** |
| Spacing between groups | **14** |
| Page policy | `Preferred, Maximum` + `AlignTop` |
| After last group | **`addStretch(1)`** |
| Each `QGroupBox` | vertical **`Maximum`** |

### Right-click action (always)

- Intro sentence + radios for what right-click / Save default engine does.
- Radio spacing **6**.

### Executables (when applicable)

- Bundled tools: checkbox  
  `Use {Tool} from the system PATH or defined Conda environment`  
  via `system_path_executable_label("Tool")`.
- Build with **`executable_checkbox_row`**: checkbox, then status line under it
  (flush with tick, spacing **2**).
- When **checked**: show resolved PATH/conda path in **grey**, or grey  
  `not found on PATH — using the built-in one` (if a bundle exists).
- When **unchecked**: **hide** the status line (no empty gap).
- Tools **without** a bundled binary (FastGA, HISAT2, …): named status always  
  **`Name`: /path** or grey **`Name`: not configured**  
  (`set_named_executable_status`).
- Long paths: **middle-elide**; full path in tooltip.
- Resolve via `resolve_system_executable` / tool helpers; refresh on Options show,
  checkbox toggle, Restore Defaults.
- Toggling PATH status must **grow/shrink the window** — never squeeze groups above
  (clear height pins before measuring).

### Process output (when applicable)

Always **`make_process_output_box(...)`**:

1. `Show process window while {tool} runs`
2. `Close process window when finished` (enabled only when 1 is on)

---

## 4. Footer

**`make_cancel_save_run_bar(dialog, left_widgets=[restore, advanced])`**

| Side | Buttons |
|---|---|
| Left | Restore Defaults, Advanced Settings ▸ (Parameters tabs only) |
| Right | **Cancel** \| **Save** \| **Run** |

- No **OK**. Spacing **8**.  
- `should_run()` ↔ `_close_action == "run"`.  
- Restore Defaults: reset fields; PATH checkboxes **off** (bundled); refresh status.

---

## 5. Height behaviour

- Width stays **608**; height follows **active tab content**.
- On show and tab change: fit to content (no blank band above the footer).
- Options after a tall Parameters tab: shrink (do not keep Parameters height).
- Advanced expand/collapse: grow/shrink; remember compact size.
- Stack/pages: vertical `Maximum` so inactive tall pages do not inflate the dialog.
- Clear pinned `maximumHeight` before re-measuring after PATH status appears.

---

## 6. Anti-patterns

- Width other than **608**, or one Settings combo wider than **260**.
- Skipping **Options**, or putting Executables / Process output above Right-click.
- Options without trailing stretch → Process output checkboxes spread apart.
- Modal `exec()` when Define inputs must accept Files clicks.
- Stock `QSpinBox`/`QComboBox` that change value on mouse wheel.
- `addRow("", radios)` without a spacer label.
- Per-dialog label width that makes one tool wider than BLAST/Align.
- Leaving Parameters height when switching to Options.
- Hand-rolled Process output or Cancel/OK footers.

---

## 7. Checklist (new function window)

- [ ] Width **608**; root margins **22/18/22/16**; root spacing **8**
- [ ] Tabs on top; compact bar; **Options** last
- [ ] Normal tab sections as needed: Mode → Inputs → Outputs → Settings
- [ ] Section separators **7** px; form H **12** / V **4**
- [ ] Fields **260**; shared label column via `sync_form_field_column_spacers`
- [ ] No-wheel spin/combo; `?` help on non-obvious rows
- [ ] Footer: Restore Defaults + Advanced Settings ▸ | Cancel Save Run
- [ ] Options: Right-click (always) → Executables? → Process output?
- [ ] PATH / named executable status (grey, elide, fit height on toggle)
- [ ] Fit-to-content on show, tab change, Advanced, PATH toggle
- [ ] Non-modal if Define inputs fills from Files panel
